const e=JSON.parse('[{"id":"LR_E4A_Q001","exercise":"exercise_4a","type":"selections","is_set":false,"question_text":"Adam, Andy, Anil, Ann, Jack, John, James and Jill want to go to a nearby city. Only two vehicles, a van and a car, are available. Only Alen and Jack know how to drive the van, hence at least one of them must be in the van. Each vehicle has a seating capacity of exactly four persons. Adam and Anil cannot go in the same vehicle and John and James must go in the same vehicle. Which of the following cannot be the list of persons who are in the car?","options":{"A":"John, James, Andy, Alen","B":"Adam, James, John, Jack","C":"Anil, James, John, Jill","D":"Anil, Andy, Jill, Alen"},"correct_answer":"A","correct_answer_value":"John, James, Andy, Alen","solution_text":"Alen or Jack or both must be in the van. Adam ≠ Anil. (A) is the answer as none of Adam and Anil is in the Car. They both are in Van which violates the given condition.","entity_count":8,"variables":2,"constraints":3,"case_splits":1,"resolution_type":"multiple","information_load":"low","solving_methodologies":["conditional_logic"],"question_operation":"statement_verification","answer_type":"mcq","difficulty":"easy","time_benchmark_seconds":90},{"id":"LR_E4A_Q002","exercise":"exercise_4a","type":"selections","is_set":false,"question_text":"A group of five is to be formed from a group of nine students A, B, C, D, E, F, G, H and I. If A is selected, then F is selected. If F is selected, then D is not selected. G is selected only if I is selected. If H is selected, then C is not selected. If B is not selected, then C is selected. If D is selected, then who among the following must be selected?","options":{"A":"C","B":"G","C":"D","D":"I"},"correct_answer":"D","correct_answer_value":"I","solution_text":"If A✓ → F✓. If F✓ → D✗. Only if I✓ → G✓. If H✓ → C✗. If B✗ → C✓. If D is selected, then F is not selected. As F is not selected, A is also not selected. Only one of H and C can be selected. So we must select I. If I is not selected, then G cannot be selected, there will be only four persons left, which means that the group cannot be formed.","entity_count":9,"variables":1,"constraints":5,"case_splits":1,"resolution_type":"multiple","information_load":"medium","solving_methodologies":["conditional_logic"],"question_operation":"hypothetical","answer_type":"mcq","difficulty":"hard","time_benchmark_seconds":150},{"id":"LR_E4A_Q003","exercise":"exercise_4a","type":"selections","is_set":false,"question_text":"Each of P, Q and R has to select two items from the six items – A, B, C, D, E and F. If P selects A, then Q does not select E. Only if R selects E, Q does not select B. If P selects D, then R will not select C. If P does not select F, then R will select B. If Q selects E, then P selects","options":{"A":"B and D.","B":"F and D.","C":"C and D.","D":"F and C."},"correct_answer":"D","correct_answer_value":"F and C.","solution_text":"As we know that Q selects E, it means P does not select A (from 1). From 2, we know that Q selects B as R does not select E. As R does not select B, it means P selects F. As P selects F, from 3, we know that R selects A. From 3, we know that if P selects D, then R does not select C which means that no one selects C, which is not possible. Hence R selects D and P selects C. The final table: P selects F, C; Q selects E, B; R selects A, D.","entity_count":3,"variables":2,"constraints":4,"case_splits":1,"resolution_type":"single","information_load":"medium","solving_methodologies":["conditional_logic","constraint_elimination"],"question_operation":"hypothetical","answer_type":"mcq","difficulty":"hard","time_benchmark_seconds":150},{"set_id":"LR_E4A_S4_6","exercise":"exercise_4a","type":"selections","is_set":true,"setup_text":"These questions are based on the following data. A team of five players is to be selected from a group of ten players − A, B, C, D, E, F, G, H, I and J. (i) Exactly one of G and H must be selected. (ii) H and A must be selected together, if selected. (iii) B and F must be selected together, if selected. (iv) F and J cannot be selected together. (v) C and D cannot be selected together.","setup_solution":"A team of five players is to be selected from a group of ten players A, B, C, D, E, F, G, H, I and J. It is given that (i) One of G and H must be selected. (ii) H and A must be selected together, and B and F must be selected together → HA and BF. (iii) F and J cannot be selected together, and C and D cannot be selected together → F ≠ J, C ≠ D.","entity_count":10,"variables":1,"constraints":5,"case_splits":2,"resolution_type":"multiple","information_load":"medium","solving_methodologies":["conditional_logic","case_elimination"],"questions":[{"id":"LR_E4A_Q004","question_text":"Which of the following statements must be true?","options":{"A":"If G is selected, then B is selected.","B":"If G is selected, then at least one of E and I is selected.","C":"If H and B are selected, then E cannot be selected.","D":"If J is not selected, then B is selected."},"correct_answer":"B","correct_answer_value":"If G is selected, then at least one of E and I is selected.","solution_text":"If G is selected, then H and A cannot be selected but B can be selected or cannot be selected. (A) is not correct. If H and B are selected, then we cannot say anything about E. (C) is incorrect. If J is selected, then we cannot say anything about B. (D) is not correct. If G is selected, then H and A cannot be selected which means that the selection can be done as follows: One of C and D can be selected and one of F and J can be selected. If F is selected then B is also selected. We can select at most one of C and D which means that one of E or I must be selected. If J is selected then F and B are not selected. We can select one of C or D in the team which means at least one of E or I must be selected. Choice (B) is correct.","question_operation":"statement_verification","answer_type":"mcq","difficulty":"hard","time_benchmark_seconds":150},{"id":"LR_E4A_Q005","question_text":"If G is selected, then which of the following can be the group of players who are not selected?","options":{"A":"H, A, F, D, I","B":"H, A, D, E, I","C":"H, C, D, J, A","D":"H, D, J, E, I"},"correct_answer":"C","correct_answer_value":"H, C, D, J, A","solution_text":"If G is selected then H and A are not selected and F is definitely selected because either H and A or B and F must be selected. So, (A) is not the answer. (B) cannot be the answer because both F and J are selected. (D) cannot be the answer because if G is selected then A definitely is not selected. So, (C) is the correct answer.","question_operation":"hypothetical","answer_type":"mcq","difficulty":"hard","time_benchmark_seconds":120},{"id":"LR_E4A_Q006","question_text":"If G is not selected and J is selected, then the total number of possible selections are","options":{"A":"Four","B":"Five","C":"Two","D":"Six"},"correct_answer":"B","correct_answer_value":"Five","solution_text":"If G is not selected and J is selected, then the total possible selections are (1) H A J E I (2) H A J C I (3) H A J D I (4) H A J C E (5) H A J D E","question_operation":"count_arrangements","answer_type":"mcq","difficulty":"hard","time_benchmark_seconds":150}]},{"set_id":"LR_E4A_S7_9","exercise":"exercise_4a","type":"selections","is_set":true,"setup_text":"These questions are based on the following information. Eleven players, out of a total of sixteen players, have to be selected for a cricket match. Among these sixteen players, there are twelve batsmen, nine bowlers and two wicketkeepers. There are six allrounders (players who can both bat and bowl are known as allrounders) and one wicket-keeper who is also a batsman. An ideal eleven consists of at least 6 batsmen, at least six bowlers and exactly one wicketkeeper. No wicket-keeper bowls.","setup_solution":"Total 16 players, out of which 11 are to be selected. Among these 16 players: number of batsmen = 12, number of bowlers = 9, number of wicket-keepers = 2, number of allrounders = 6 (out of 12 batsmen and 9 bowlers), number of wicket-keeper + batsman = 1. Now, number of only wicket-keeper = 2 – 1 = 1. Number of only batsman = 11 – 6 = 5 (Eleven, because one batsman is wicket keeper). Number of only bowlers = 9 – 6 = 3.","entity_count":16,"variables":2,"constraints":3,"case_splits":2,"resolution_type":"multiple","information_load":"high","solving_methodologies":["combinatorial_counting","constraint_elimination"],"type_specific":{"note":"Requires deriving entity counts from overlapping categories (batsmen who are also allrounders, wicket-keeper who is also a batsman) before any selection logic can be applied. The setup itself is an arithmetic derivation step, not just a constraint list."},"questions":[{"id":"LR_E4A_Q007","question_text":"If the wicket-keeper, who is also a batsman, is selected in the ideal eleven, then what is the minimum possible number of players in the team who can only bowl?","options":{"A":"Zero","B":"One","C":"Two","D":"More than two"},"correct_answer":"A","correct_answer_value":"Zero","solution_text":"Ideal Eleven: If all the 6 bowlers are also batsmen (i.e., 6 allrounders), plus one wicket-keeper batsman, gives 7 players. Thus, the least number of only bowlers will be zero.","question_operation":"count_arrangements","answer_type":"mcq","difficulty":"hard","time_benchmark_seconds":120},{"id":"LR_E4A_Q008","question_text":"If the number of allrounders should be kept at a minimum while selecting the team, then what is the least number of players who can only bat?","options":{"A":"Six","B":"Five","C":"Four","D":"None of these"},"correct_answer":"C","correct_answer_value":"Four","solution_text":"As there are 3 players who can only bowl, but at least 6 bowlers are required, hence minimum number of allrounders = 3. The wicket-keeper selected is a batsman. Hence, three bowlers who can only bowl. Hence, the team consists of 3 bowlers + 3 allrounders + 1 wicket keeper = 7. But the total number of players who can only bat is (11 – 7) = 4.","question_operation":"count_arrangements","answer_type":"mcq","difficulty":"hard","time_benchmark_seconds":150},{"id":"LR_E4A_Q009","question_text":"Which of the following statements is never true?","options":{"A":"All the eleven players can bat in a team.","B":"In a team, 8 players can bat and 8 players can bowl.","C":"In a team, 7 players can bat and 7 players can bowl.","D":"In a team, when the number of allrounders is kept at a minimum, then the number of players who can only bat is less to those who can only bowl."},"correct_answer":"D","correct_answer_value":"In a team, when the number of allrounders is kept at a minimum, then the number of players who can only bat is less to those who can only bowl.","solution_text":"(A) If all eleven are batsmen, then the wicket-keeper who can also bat must be selected, along with 6 allrounders (so we can have six bowlers) and 4 only batsman. (B) For 8 players to bat and 8 players to bowl, we can have: Only batsman = 2, Allrounders = 6, Only bowler = 2, Only wicket-keeper = 1. (C) For 7 players to bat and 7 to bowl: Allrounders = 4, Only batsman = 3, Only bowler = 3, Only wicket-keeper = 1. (D) The number of allrounders = 3 (3 is the minimum). Now, the number of only batsman can NEVER be less than the number of only bowlers, as out of these 8 remaining players, one is a wicket-keeper, and the number of only bowlers cannot be more than 3.","question_operation":"statement_verification","answer_type":"mcq","difficulty":"hard","time_benchmark_seconds":150}]},{"set_id":"LR_E4A_S10_12","exercise":"exercise_4a","type":"selections","is_set":true,"setup_text":"These questions are based on the following information. A team of three persons is to be selected from a group of five persons – A, B, C, D and E under the following constraints. (i) If A is selected, then B must be selected. (ii) If C is not selected, then E must be selected.","setup_solution":"From (i), A and B can be selected as follows: Both A and B are selected, or Only B is selected, or Neither A nor B is selected. From (ii), C and E can be selected as follows: Only E is selected, or Only C is selected, or Both E and C are selected.","entity_count":5,"variables":1,"constraints":2,"case_splits":1,"resolution_type":"multiple","resolution_count":6,"information_load":"low","solving_methodologies":["conditional_logic","combinatorial_counting"],"questions":[{"id":"LR_E4A_Q010","question_text":"In how many ways can the team be selected?","options":{"A":"Eight","B":"Six","C":"Seven","D":"None of these"},"correct_answer":"B","correct_answer_value":"Six","solution_text":"From the above explanation, it is clear that at least one among C and E must be selected. If only C is selected, the possibilities are (1) C, A, B (2) C, B, D. If only E is selected the possibilities are (3) E, A, B (4) E, B, D. If both C and E are selected, the possibilities are (5) C, E, D (6) C, E, B. There are 6 possible ways.","question_operation":"count_arrangements","answer_type":"mcq","difficulty":"medium","time_benchmark_seconds":120},{"id":"LR_E4A_Q011","question_text":"If D is not selected, then who must always be selected?","options":{"A":"A","B":"B","C":"C","D":"E"},"correct_answer":"B","correct_answer_value":"B","solution_text":"From the above solution, if D is not selected, then B must always be selected.","question_operation":"hypothetical","answer_type":"mcq","difficulty":"medium","time_benchmark_seconds":75},{"id":"LR_E4A_Q012","question_text":"Which of the following is not a possible team?","options":{"A":"C, E, D","B":"E, A, B.","C":"C, B, D","D":"A, B, D"},"correct_answer":"D","correct_answer_value":"A, B, D","solution_text":"A, B, D is not a possible team.","question_operation":"statement_verification","answer_type":"mcq","difficulty":"medium","time_benchmark_seconds":75}]},{"set_id":"LR_E4A_S13_15","exercise":"exercise_4a","type":"selections","is_set":true,"setup_text":"These questions are based on the following information. A team of four persons is to be selected from seven persons – Anuj, Bindu, Chanti, Dheeraj, Eswar, Farhaan and Ganesh under the following constraints. (i) At most two of Chanti, Eswar and Ganesh can be selected. (ii) Atleast one of Anuj and Bindu must be selected. (iii) If Farhaan is selected, then neither Anuj nor Chanti can be selected.","setup_solution":"Let each person be denoted by the first letter of his/her name. From (iii), if F is selected, then A and C are not selected. From (ii) One among A and B must be selected. The possibilities are: If F is selected then, (a) F, B, E, G (b) F, B, E, D (c) F, B, D, G. If F is not selected, then A or B or A, B must be selected in the team as we have to select 4, we have to reject 3 and among C, E and G atleast one must be rejected. From (i), at most two of C, E and G can be selected. The possibilities are: (d) A, B, C, E (e) A, B, C, G (f) A, B, G, E (g) A, B, D, C (h) A, B, D, E (i) A, B, D, G (j) A, D, C, E (k) A, D, C, G (l) A, D, G, E (m) B, D, C, E (n) B, D, C, G (o) B, D, G, E","entity_count":7,"variables":1,"constraints":3,"case_splits":2,"resolution_type":"multiple","resolution_count":15,"information_load":"medium","solving_methodologies":["combinatorial_counting","conditional_logic"],"questions":[{"id":"LR_E4A_Q013","question_text":"If Dheeraj is selected, then in how many ways can the team be selected?","options":{"A":"Eight","B":"Ten","C":"Nine","D":"Eleven"},"correct_answer":"D","correct_answer_value":"Eleven","solution_text":"Except possibilities (a), (d), (e) and (f) all other teams have Dheeraj.","question_operation":"count_arrangements","answer_type":"mcq","difficulty":"hard","time_benchmark_seconds":150},{"id":"LR_E4A_Q014","question_text":"If atmost one of Farhaan and Ganesh can be selected, then in how many ways can the team be selected?","options":{"A":"11","B":"12","C":"13","D":"14"},"correct_answer":"C","correct_answer_value":"13","solution_text":"Except (a) and (c), all have at most one of F and G.","question_operation":"count_arrangements","answer_type":"mcq","difficulty":"hard","time_benchmark_seconds":150},{"id":"LR_E4A_Q015","question_text":"If Eswar is not selected, then in how many ways can the team be selected?","options":{"A":"Six","B":"Seven","C":"Eight","D":"Nine"},"correct_answer":"A","correct_answer_value":"Six","solution_text":"(c), (e), (g), (i), (k) and (n) are the possibilities.","question_operation":"count_arrangements","answer_type":"mcq","difficulty":"hard","time_benchmark_seconds":150}]},{"set_id":"LR_E4A_S16_19","exercise":"exercise_4a","type":"selections","is_set":true,"setup_text":"These questions are based on the following information. A team of delegates has to be formed from a group of ten people, N through W, subject to the following conditions. (i) If Q is selected, then none among U, V or W can be selected. Also U, V and W cannot be selected together. (ii) If R is selected, then either S or T must be selected. But S and T cannot be selected together. (iii) At least one out of N, O and P must be selected. (iv) If P is selected, then neither N nor O can be selected. (v) N and R cannot be selected together. (vi) N and Q cannot be selected together. (vii) P and V cannot be selected together. (viii) P and W cannot be selected together.","setup_solution":"From (i) the pairs QV, QU, QW cannot be selected together. Also UVW cannot be selected together. From (ii) the possibilities are RS, RT, only S or only T. From (iii) and (iv), among the possibilities - only N, only O, only P, or only N and O – one must happen. From (v) to (viii) the pairs NR, NQ, PV and PW should not be selected together.","entity_count":10,"variables":1,"constraints":8,"case_splits":3,"resolution_type":"multiple","information_load":"high","solving_methodologies":["conditional_logic","combinatorial_counting"],"questions":[{"id":"LR_E4A_Q016","question_text":"If a team of four is selected and Q being one of them, then which of the following must be selected?","options":{"A":"R","B":"O","C":"T","D":"S"},"correct_answer":"A","correct_answer_value":"R","solution_text":"If Q is selected, none among N, V, U or W can be selected. Among the remaining, one among O and P will be selected. The remaining two members have to be selected from R, S and T. S and T cannot be selected, hence R must be a part of the team.","question_operation":"hypothetical","answer_type":"mcq","difficulty":"hard","time_benchmark_seconds":120},{"id":"LR_E4A_Q017","question_text":"What is the maximum possible size of a selected team?","options":{"A":"Four","B":"Five","C":"Six","D":"Seven"},"correct_answer":"B","correct_answer_value":"Five","solution_text":"The maximum number of selections in the team can be as shown below. (a) N, O, two people out of (U, V, W) and one person out of (S, T). (b) O, two people out of (U, V, W), R and one person out of (S, T). Hence the maximum team size is five.","question_operation":"count_arrangements","answer_type":"mcq","difficulty":"hard","time_benchmark_seconds":150},{"id":"LR_E4A_Q018","question_text":"What is the maximum possible size of the team if P is selected?","options":{"A":"Four","B":"Five","C":"Six","D":"Seven"},"correct_answer":"A","correct_answer_value":"Four","solution_text":"If P is selected, the maximum selections in the team can be as shown below. (a) P, Q, R, S (b) P, Q, R, T. Hence the maximum team size is four.","question_operation":"hypothetical","answer_type":"mcq","difficulty":"hard","time_benchmark_seconds":120},{"id":"LR_E4A_Q019","question_text":"In how many different ways can the team be selected if Q is selected?","options":{"A":"Seven","B":"Eight","C":"Nine","D":"Ten"},"correct_answer":"D","correct_answer_value":"Ten","solution_text":"If Q is selected the number of ways the team can be selected is: (a) O, Q, R, S (b) O, Q, R, T (c) O, Q, S (d) O, Q, T (e) P, Q, R, S (f) P, Q, R, T (g) P, Q, S (h) P, Q, T (i) Q, O (j) Q, P. Hence the team can be selected in ten ways.","question_operation":"count_arrangements","answer_type":"mcq","difficulty":"hard","time_benchmark_seconds":180}]},{"set_id":"LR_E4A_S20_22","exercise":"exercise_4a","type":"selections","is_set":true,"setup_text":"These questions are based on the following information. Vijay asked Ajay to select 6 pens of different colours from the available ten colours – Orange, Red, Blue, White, Pink, Yellow, Black, Grey, Violet and Brown. Vijay has laid down some conditions for Ajay, as given below: (i) If Ajay selects the Blue pen, then he must select the Orange pen also, and vice versa. (ii) If Ajay selects the Grey pen, then he must select the Black pen also, and vice versa. (iii) If Ajay selects the Yellow pen, then he cannot select the Grey pen. (iv) Exactly one of Red and Violet pens must be selected.","setup_solution":"It is given that (i) If Ajay selects the Blue pen, then he selects the Orange pen also and vice-versa. (ii) If he selects the Grey pen, then he selects the Black pen also and vice-versa. (iii) If Ajay selects the Yellow pen, then he cannot select the Grey pen. (iv) Exactly one of Red and Violet pens must be selected.","entity_count":10,"variables":1,"constraints":4,"case_splits":2,"resolution_type":"multiple","information_load":"medium","solving_methodologies":["conditional_logic","constraint_elimination"],"questions":[{"id":"LR_E4A_Q020","question_text":"If Ajay does not select the Grey or the Brown pen, then among the following choices he can reject the","options":{"A":"Pink pen.","B":"White pen.","C":"Red pen.","D":"Orange pen."},"correct_answer":"C","correct_answer_value":"Red pen.","solution_text":"If he did not select Grey and Brown, he must select White, Pink, Orange, Blue, Yellow, Red/Violet. He can reject Red.","question_operation":"hypothetical","answer_type":"mcq","difficulty":"medium","time_benchmark_seconds":90},{"id":"LR_E4A_Q021","question_text":"Which of the following can be the list of colours of pens selected by Ajay?","options":{"A":"Yellow, Pink, White, Blue, Brown, Orange.","B":"Red, Blue, Orange, White, Grey, Yellow.","C":"Black, Grey, Brown, Violet, Pink, White.","D":"Red, Pink, Blue, Orange, Violet, White."},"correct_answer":"C","correct_answer_value":"Black, Grey, Brown, Violet, Pink, White.","solution_text":"(A) is not the answer, as there is neither the Red nor the Violet coloured pens. (B) is not the answer, as both the Yellow and the grey coloured pens are selected. (D) is not the correct answer, as both the Red and the Violet coloured pens are selected.","question_operation":"statement_verification","answer_type":"mcq","difficulty":"medium","time_benchmark_seconds":90},{"id":"LR_E4A_Q022","question_text":"Which of the following can confirm the selection of pens?","options":{"A":"Blue and Yellow pens are selected.","B":"Red and Grey pens are selected.","C":"Orange and Red pens are not selected.","D":"Grey pen is not selected, but the Orange pen is selected."},"correct_answer":"C","correct_answer_value":"Orange and Red pens are not selected.","solution_text":"If the Orange coloured pen is not selected, then the Blue coloured pen also cannot be selected. If the Red coloured pen is not selected, then the Violet coloured pen should be selected. Hence, there are seven coloured pens out of which Ajay has to select six coloured pens. He must select the Grey coloured pen and he cannot select the Yellow coloured pen. The six coloured pens he selects are White, Pink, Black, Grey, Violet and Brown.","question_operation":"identify_completing_statement","answer_type":"mcq","difficulty":"hard","time_benchmark_seconds":150}]},{"set_id":"LR_E4A_S23_26","exercise":"exercise_4a","type":"selections","is_set":true,"setup_text":"These questions are based on the following data. Four teams are to be formed from fourteen persons. A team must consist of at least two persons and no two teams can have the same number of persons. Each person can be a member of exactly one team. Each of Rama, Ramya, Radha and Raksha must be a member of a different team. Each of Rohini, Padma, Priya and Priyanka must be a member of a different team. Pratima, Pratibha and Sudha must be in the same team. Shreya and Shalini must be in the same team. Rama cannot be in the same team with any of Padma, Priya and Priyanka. Ramya can be in the same team with neither Priyanka nor Priya. Radha cannot be in the same team with Priyanka. Swetha is in one of the teams.","setup_solution":"Each team must consist of a minimum of two members and each of the four teams must have a distinct number of members. This implies the number of persons in different teams must be 2, 3, 4 and 5. Each of Rama, Ramya, Radha and Raksha must be in a different team. Each of Rohini, Padma, Priya and Priyanka must be in a different team. From conditions, one each of Rama, Ramya, Radha, Raksha must be paired with one each of Rohini, Padma, Priya and Priyanka. Priyanka cannot be paired with Rama, Ramya or Radha, which implies that Priyanka is paired with Raksha. Using a similar logic: Rama and Rohini, Ramya and Padma, Radha and Priya are paired together. Pratima, Pratibha and Sudha must be in a team together but since all teams already have two members each, these people can only be accommodated in the team that has five members in it. Shreya and Shalini must be in a team together which means they can only be accommodated in a team that has four members in it. Swetha can only be placed in the team that has three members in it. Teams: (2 members), (3 members with Swetha), (4 members with Shreya and Shalini), V (5 members with Pratima, Pratibha and Sudha).","entity_count":14,"variables":2,"constraints":8,"case_splits":1,"resolution_type":"multiple","resolution_count":24,"information_load":"high","solving_methodologies":["constraint_elimination","combinatorial_counting"],"questions":[{"id":"LR_E4A_Q023","question_text":"How many possible ways are there to form the four teams?","options":{"A":"24","B":"120","C":"64","D":"6"},"correct_answer":"A","correct_answer_value":"24","solution_text":"There are 4 pairs i.e., Raksha-Priyanka, Rama-Rohini, Ramya-Padma, Radha-Priya who must be allocated to 4 teams which can be done in 4! ways. 4! = 24 ways.","question_operation":"count_arrangements","answer_type":"mcq","difficulty":"hard","time_benchmark_seconds":150},{"id":"LR_E4A_Q024","question_text":"Which of the following statements is not definitely true?","options":{"A":"Swetha is in a three member team.","B":"There is a two member team.","C":"Sudha is in a five member team.","D":"Shreya is in the two member team."},"correct_answer":"D","correct_answer_value":"Shreya is in the two member team.","solution_text":"We can see that statements made in choices (A), (B) and (C) are true as per the above discussion. Shreya is in a four member team, hence, choice (D) is definitely not true.","question_operation":"statement_verification","answer_type":"mcq","difficulty":"hard","time_benchmark_seconds":120},{"id":"LR_E4A_Q025","question_text":"Which of the following additional statements is sufficient to know the composition of teams?","options":{"A":"Rohini and Padma are in teams with five and four members respectively and Radha is not in a three member team.","B":"Sudha and Shalini are in teams with five and four members respectively and Swetha is not in a two member team.","C":"Pratima and Swetha are in teams with five and three members respectively and Shreya is not in a two member team.","D":"None of these"},"correct_answer":"A","correct_answer_value":"Rohini and Padma are in teams with five and four members respectively and Radha is not in a three member team.","solution_text":"As per choice (A), if Rohini is in a team of five members, it means that Rama is also in that team. Padma is in a four member team implies that Ramya is also in that team and Radha is not in a three member team implies that she is in a two member team along with Priya which leaves us with Priyanka and Raksha in a three member team which completes the arrangement. Hence, choice (A) gives us the complete arrangement.","question_operation":"identify_completing_statement","answer_type":"mcq","difficulty":"hard","time_benchmark_seconds":180},{"id":"LR_E4A_Q026","question_text":"Who of the following must be a member of a five member team?","options":{"A":"Priya","B":"Priyanka","C":"Pratima","D":"Shreya"},"correct_answer":"C","correct_answer_value":"Pratima","solution_text":"Pratima is a member of the five member team.","question_operation":"position_lookup","answer_type":"mcq","difficulty":"medium","time_benchmark_seconds":75}]},{"set_id":"LR_E4A_S27_30","exercise":"exercise_4a","type":"selections","is_set":true,"setup_text":"These questions are based on the following data. A cricket team consisting of 11 players has to be selected from amongst 16 players, A through P. Among these 16 players (a) A, C, E, G, I, K, M, J and O are batsmen. (b) B, D, F, G, H, J, M and P are bowlers. (c) L and N are wicket-keepers. (d) Any player who is both a bowler and a batsman is called an allrounder. The Captain and the Vice-Captain are the allrounders. The team is selected as per the following restrictions. (1) The team should contain 5 batsmen, 3 bowlers, 2 allrounders and a wicket-keeper and the Captain and the Vice-Captain must be selected. (2) Neither G nor M is the Captain and neither J nor G is the Vice-Captain. (3) The players mentioned in the following pairs must not get selected together: J and N; B and F; D and H; D and P; E and I; A and E; and B and C.","setup_solution":"It is given that A, C, E, G, I, K, M, J and O are batsmen, B, D, F, G, H, J, M and P are bowlers, L and N are wicket-keepers. The players who are both bowlers and batsmen are known as allrounders. Hence G, M and J are allrounders. The Captain and the Vice-Captain are allrounders. Neither G nor M is the Captain, that means J is the Captain. Similarly M is the Vice-Captain. As only two allrounders are to be selected, J and M are selected and G cannot be selected. Five batsmen are to be selected from A, C, E, I, K and O. It is also given that if E is selected, then A and I cannot be selected which means that 5 batsmen cannot be selected. Therefore, E should not be selected and the batsmen selected are A, C, I, K and O. It is given that three bowlers are to be selected from B, D, F, H and P. It is also given that if D is selected, P and H cannot be selected and the bowlers selected would be B, D, F which is not a feasible combination (as B and F cannot be together). Therefore, D is not selected. We already know that C is selected, hence B cannot be selected. The bowlers who are selected are F, H and P. J and N cannot be selected. As J is already selected as the Captain, hence N cannot be selected into the team. Therefore, L is selected as the wicket-keeper. The 11 players who are selected into the team are J(Captain), M(Vice-Captain), L(Wicket Keeper), O, F, H, P, A, C, I, K.","entity_count":16,"variables":2,"constraints":10,"case_splits":1,"resolution_type":"single","information_load":"high","solving_methodologies":["constraint_elimination","case_elimination"],"questions":[{"id":"LR_E4A_Q027","question_text":"Which two players are the Captain and the Vice-Captain of the team respectively?","options":{"A":"J and G","B":"G and M","C":"J and M","D":"G and K"},"correct_answer":"C","correct_answer_value":"J and M","solution_text":"J and M are the Captain and the Vice-Captain of the team respectively.","question_operation":"position_lookup","answer_type":"mcq","difficulty":"hard","time_benchmark_seconds":90},{"id":"LR_E4A_Q028","question_text":"Who are the three bowlers selected in the team?","options":{"A":"F, H and P","B":"D, F and H","C":"F, H and B","D":"B, D and F"},"correct_answer":"A","correct_answer_value":"F, H and P","solution_text":"F, H and P are the three bowlers selected in the team.","question_operation":"position_lookup","answer_type":"mcq","difficulty":"hard","time_benchmark_seconds":90},{"id":"LR_E4A_Q029","question_text":"Which of the following is definitely false?","options":{"A":"J, O, P, A, L and I are selected.","B":"L, O, F, H and C are not selected.","C":"B, D, E and N are not selected.","D":"M, I, K, P and O are selected."},"correct_answer":"B","correct_answer_value":"L, O, F, H and C are not selected.","solution_text":"L, O, F, H and C are not selected is definitely false.","question_operation":"statement_verification","answer_type":"mcq","difficulty":"hard","time_benchmark_seconds":90},{"id":"LR_E4A_Q030","question_text":"If after the first match, in every following match, the Captain and the Vice-Captain exchange their job-responsibilities (i.e., Captain takes up the Vice-Captaincy and the Vice-Captain takes up the Captaincy), then who would be the Vice-Captain in the 86th match?","options":{"A":"J","B":"M","C":"Either J or M","D":"L"},"correct_answer":"A","correct_answer_value":"J","solution_text":"In the 2nd match J is the Vice-Captain and M is the Captain. As, 86th match is an even numbered match, J will be the Vice-Captain in that match.","question_operation":"hypothetical","answer_type":"mcq","difficulty":"hard","time_benchmark_seconds":90}]},{"set_id":"LR_E4B_S1_3","exercise":"exercise_4b","type":"selections","is_set":true,"setup_text":"These questions are based on the following data. In a class of ten students − A, B, C, D, E, F, G, H, I and J, ranks are given to the top five students, such that the student who gets the highest marks will get the 1st rank, student getting the second highest marks will get the 2nd rank and so on. It is also known that no two students get equal marks. D gets less marks than G and H gets less marks than I. If F gets a rank, then D will not get a rank. Exactly one of B and G gets a rank. If I gets a rank, then C will get a rank, and vice-versa.","setup_solution":"(1) D < G and H < I. If D gets rank, then G also gets a rank and If H gets a rank, then I also gets a rank. (2) F ≠ D. (3) B/G (Only one of the two). (4) I ↔ C (If I gets a rank then, C will also get a rank. If I gets a rank, both I and C get ranks.)","entity_count":10,"variables":1,"constraints":4,"case_splits":2,"resolution_type":"multiple","information_load":"high","solving_methodologies":["conditional_logic","case_elimination"],"questions":[{"id":"LR_E4B_Q001","question_text":"If E did not get a rank and I got less marks than F, then which of the following is definitely false?","options":{"A":"J or A gets a rank.","B":"D gets a rank.","C":"B gets a rank.","D":"F gets a rank."},"correct_answer":"B","correct_answer_value":"D gets a rank.","solution_text":"It is given that E did not get a rank and that F got more marks than I, which means that F > I > H. So if F does not get a rank, then none of I or H gets a rank. If I does not get a rank, then C also does not get a rank, which means that A, B, D, G and J get ranks. However, this is not possible as only one out of B or G gets a rank, but not both, as per the given conditions. This means that F has to get a rank, which means that D will not get a rank.","question_operation":"hypothetical","answer_type":"mcq","difficulty":"hard","time_benchmark_seconds":150},{"id":"LR_E4B_Q002","question_text":"If D and H got two consecutive ranks, then C would not get the","options":{"A":"1st rank.","B":"2nd rank.","C":"3rd rank.","D":"4th rank."},"correct_answer":"D","correct_answer_value":"4th rank.","solution_text":"If D and H get ranks, then G, I and C should also get ranks because G got more marks than D and I got more than H. If I gets a rank, then C also should get a rank. As D and H got two successive ranks, G and I must always be ranked higher than D and H. So D and H gets either 3rd or 4th rank or 4th or 5th rank. Hence, C would not get the 4th rank.","question_operation":"hypothetical","answer_type":"mcq","difficulty":"hard","time_benchmark_seconds":150},{"id":"LR_E4B_Q003","question_text":"If F is not ranked and H gets more marks than G, then who among the following must be ranked?","options":{"A":"C","B":"G","C":"A or E or J","D":"B"},"correct_answer":"A","correct_answer_value":"C","solution_text":"If F is not ranked and H got more marks than G, then H and I both are selected. If I is selected C must be selected.","question_operation":"hypothetical","answer_type":"mcq","difficulty":"hard","time_benchmark_seconds":120}]},{"set_id":"LR_E4B_S4_6","exercise":"exercise_4b","type":"selections","is_set":true,"setup_text":"These questions are based on the following information. Mr. Forest wants to pack his bag. He wants to pack at least one item among – glue, paper, lantern, candle, matchstick, lighter, medicine, mosquito net and snacks. He packed his bag as per the instructions given by his mother which are given below. (i) If he is carrying a match stick, he should also carry a lighter. (ii) Paper and glue cannot be taken together. (iii) He must carry medicine. (iv) Mosquito net cannot be taken with lighter or lantern. (v) He must take either a lantern or a candle. (vi) Matchstick and lighter serve the same purpose. Similarly, lantern and candle serve the same purpose. (vii) He must carry either a matchstick or a lighter.","setup_solution":"From (ii), only one among paper and glue can be taken. From (iv), if he packs mosquito net, then he cannot pack lighter or lantern. If the mosquito net is not packed, then lighter and lantern can be taken. At most, seven items can be taken.","entity_count":9,"variables":1,"constraints":7,"case_splits":2,"resolution_type":"multiple","information_load":"medium","solving_methodologies":["conditional_logic","combinatorial_counting"],"questions":[{"id":"LR_E4B_Q004","question_text":"What is the maximum possible number of items that can be packed in the bag?","options":{"A":"Seven","B":"Eight","C":"Six","D":"None of these"},"correct_answer":"A","correct_answer_value":"Seven","solution_text":"From (ii), only one among paper and glue can be taken. From (iv), if he packs mosquito net, then he cannot pack lighter or lantern. If the mosquito net is not packed, then lighter and lantern can be taken. At most, seven items can be taken.","question_operation":"count_arrangements","answer_type":"mcq","difficulty":"medium","time_benchmark_seconds":120},{"id":"LR_E4B_Q005","question_text":"If he carries five items, then in how many possible ways can he select the items considering his intension to pack such items which would serve the maximum possible number of purposes?","options":{"A":"Three","B":"Four","C":"Six","D":"None of these"},"correct_answer":"B","correct_answer_value":"Four","solution_text":"He cannot take mosquito net. As, he wants maximum possible number of purposes to be served, he must take only one of matchstick and lighter. From (i), he must pack lighter. From (v), he would pack one of candle and lantern. From (ii) he would pack one of glue and paper. Hence, the possible number of ways are: (i) Snacks, Medicine, Lighter, Lantern, Glue (ii) Snacks, Medicine, Lighter, Lantern, Paper (iii) Snacks, Medicine, Lighter, Candle, Glue (iv) Snacks, Medicine, Lighter, Candle, Paper. There are four possible ways.","question_operation":"count_arrangements","answer_type":"mcq","difficulty":"hard","time_benchmark_seconds":150},{"id":"LR_E4B_Q006","question_text":"If he carries five items with him which item will he definitely not carry, considering his intention to carry such items which would serve maximum possible number of purposes?","options":{"A":"Matchstick and Glue","B":"Mosquito net Candle, Paper and Matchstick","C":"Mosquito net and Matchstick","D":"None of these"},"correct_answer":"C","correct_answer_value":"Mosquito net and Matchstick","solution_text":"He will not carry mosquito net and matchstick.","question_operation":"statement_verification","answer_type":"mcq","difficulty":"hard","time_benchmark_seconds":120}]},{"set_id":"LR_E4B_S7_10","exercise":"exercise_4b","type":"selections","is_set":true,"setup_text":"These questions are based on the following information. A group of four persons is to be selected from eight persons – Agni, Ravi, Tarum, Daman, Mohan, Nikesh, Lalit and Bindu, under the following conditions. (i) Nikesh and Ravi cannot be selected together. (ii) At least, one between Tarun and Lalit must be selected. (iii) At most, one among Agni, Daman and Bindu can be selected. (iv) Unless Mohan is selected, Tarun cannot be selected.","setup_solution":"Let us represent each person with the first letter of his name. From (i), N and R cannot be selected together implies, either only N can be selected or only R can be selected or neither of them is selected. From (ii), either both of T and L are selected or one among them is selected. From (iii), either none of A, D and B is selected or only one among A, D and B is selected. From (iv), among M and T, either both are selected or neither is selected or only M is selected. As, two among A, D and B would definitely be not selected and among N and R at least one would not be selected. Among T, L and M at least two must be selected. M must always be selected.","entity_count":8,"variables":1,"constraints":4,"case_splits":2,"resolution_type":"multiple","information_load":"medium","solving_methodologies":["conditional_logic","combinatorial_counting"],"questions":[{"id":"LR_E4B_Q007","question_text":"Who must always be there in the team?","options":{"A":"Mohan","B":"Tarun","C":"Lalit","D":"More than one of the above"},"correct_answer":"A","correct_answer_value":"Mohan","solution_text":"Mohan must always be there in the team.","question_operation":"position_lookup","answer_type":"mcq","difficulty":"medium","time_benchmark_seconds":90},{"id":"LR_E4B_Q008","question_text":"Which of the following is not a possible team?","options":{"A":"Mohan, Tarun, Lalit, Agni","B":"Nikesh, Mohan, Tarun, Daman","C":"Bindu, Nikesh, Mohan, Lalit","D":"Lalit, Nikesh, Tarun, Bindu"},"correct_answer":"D","correct_answer_value":"Lalit, Nikesh, Tarun, Bindu","solution_text":"Choice (D) violates condition (iv).","question_operation":"statement_verification","answer_type":"mcq","difficulty":"medium","time_benchmark_seconds":75},{"id":"LR_E4B_Q009","question_text":"In how many ways can the team be selected, if Lalit is not selected?","options":{"A":"Eight","B":"Six","C":"Ten","D":"None of these"},"correct_answer":"B","correct_answer_value":"Six","solution_text":"As M must be selected, among T and L at least one would be selected. As L is not selected, M and T are selected. The possible teams are as follows. (i) M, T, A, N (ii) M, T, A, R (iii) M, T, D, N (iv) M, T, D, R (v) M, T, B, N (vi) M, T, B, R. There are 6 possible ways.","question_operation":"count_arrangements","answer_type":"mcq","difficulty":"hard","time_benchmark_seconds":150},{"id":"LR_E4B_Q010","question_text":"Which of the following conditions would help to get only one possible way to select the team?","options":{"A":"Tarun and Daman should always be selected together.","B":"At most, one among Agni and Rani can be selected.","C":"Unless Agni is selected, Nikesh is not to be selected.","D":"None of these"},"correct_answer":"D","correct_answer_value":"None of these","solution_text":"Among the given conditions, none can help to get only one possible way to select the team.","question_operation":"identify_completing_statement","answer_type":"mcq","difficulty":"hard","time_benchmark_seconds":120}]},{"set_id":"LR_E4B_S11_13","exercise":"exercise_4b","type":"selections","is_set":true,"setup_text":"These questions are based on the following information. Three girls – Anjali, Bharathi and Chandrika and four boys – Kiran, Lala, Manoj and Naveen are to be divided into two teams under the following constraints. (i) Each team must have at least one girl and at least one boy and at least three persons in total. (ii) If Anjali and Bharathi are selected in a team, then the team must have only one boy. (iii) Kiran and Lala cannot be in the same team. (iv) Chandrika and Naveen can be in the same team, only if Bharathi is selected in that team.","setup_solution":"Let each person be denoted by the first letter of his/her name.","entity_count":7,"variables":1,"constraints":4,"case_splits":2,"resolution_type":"multiple","information_load":"high","solving_methodologies":["conditional_logic","combinatorial_counting"],"questions":[{"id":"LR_E4B_Q011","question_text":"If Kiran and Chandrika are in the same team, then in how many ways can the other team be selected?","options":{"A":"Six","B":"Three","C":"Four","D":"Five"},"correct_answer":"D","correct_answer_value":"Five","solution_text":"K and C are in the same team. L must be in the other team (from (iii)). If A and B are in the same team as L, then it violates (iv) (from (ii)). Only one of A and B is in the same team as L. Using other conditions the possibilities are: (a) K, C, A, M and L, B, N (b) K, C, B, M and L, A, N (c) K, C, A and L, M, N, B (d) K, C, B and L, M, N, A (e) K, C, B, N and L, M, A","question_operation":"count_arrangements","answer_type":"mcq","difficulty":"hard","time_benchmark_seconds":150},{"id":"LR_E4B_Q012","question_text":"If Manoj is not in the same team as Bharathi, then in how many ways can the teams be selected?","options":{"A":"Three","B":"Four","C":"Five","D":"Six"},"correct_answer":"D","correct_answer_value":"Six","solution_text":"M and B are not in the same team. From (iii), either K or L is with B. Now, if A is with B, then C and N must be with M, which violates (iv). A is with M. Now, atleast one of C and N is with B. The teams are: B, K/L, C, N and M, L/K, A; B, K/L, C and M, L/K, A, N; B, K/L, N and M, L/K, A, C. There are six possibilities.","question_operation":"count_arrangements","answer_type":"mcq","difficulty":"hard","time_benchmark_seconds":150},{"id":"LR_E4B_Q013","question_text":"If three boys are selected into one team, then in how many ways can the teams be selected?","options":{"A":"Four","B":"Five","C":"Three","D":"Six"},"correct_answer":"A","correct_answer_value":"Four","solution_text":"From (iii), M and N are in the same team. One of K and L is with them. C cannot be with them as it violates (iv). From (ii), only one of A and B is with them. The possibilities are: M, N, K/L, A/B and L/K, C, B/A. There are four possibilities.","question_operation":"count_arrangements","answer_type":"mcq","difficulty":"hard","time_benchmark_seconds":150}]},{"set_id":"LR_E4B_S14_15","exercise":"exercise_4b","type":"selections","is_set":true,"setup_text":"These questions are based on the following information. A team is to be selected from eight persons – P, Q, R, S, T, U, V and W under the following constraints. (i) Atleast one of P, Q and R must be selected. (ii) At most two of S, T and U can be selected. (iii) V and W cannot be selected together. (iv) If one of Q, S and V is selected, then the other two must not be selected. (v) If one of R, U and W is selected, then the other two must be selected.","setup_solution":"From (ii), atleast one of S, T, U must not be selected. From (iii), atleast one of V and W must not be selected. From (iv), atleast two of Q, S, V must not be selected. From (v), either all of R, U and W are selected or none of R, U and W is selected.","entity_count":8,"variables":1,"constraints":5,"case_splits":2,"resolution_type":"multiple","information_load":"high","solving_methodologies":["conditional_logic","combinatorial_counting"],"questions":[{"id":"LR_E4B_Q014","question_text":"What can be the maximum size of the team?","options":{"A":"Six","B":"Five","C":"Four","D":"Three"},"correct_answer":"A","correct_answer_value":"Six","solution_text":"To maximize, we have to select R, U and W. V is not selected. S or T can be selected. From (iv), we take Q is selected. T is also selected. P can also be selected. Violating none of the conditions, we can select PQRTUW. There can be 6 people.","question_operation":"count_arrangements","answer_type":"mcq","difficulty":"hard","time_benchmark_seconds":150},{"id":"LR_E4B_Q015","question_text":"If W is selected, then at most how many more persons can be selected along with him?","options":{"A":"Six","B":"Five","C":"Four","D":"Three"},"correct_answer":"B","correct_answer_value":"Five","solution_text":"From the above solution, we can say that at most five can be selected with him.","question_operation":"count_arrangements","answer_type":"mcq","difficulty":"hard","time_benchmark_seconds":120}]},{"set_id":"LR_E4B_S16_19","exercise":"exercise_4b","type":"selections","is_set":true,"setup_text":"These questions are based on the following information. A team of five delegates must be selected from a group of Americans (Jack, Michael, Brenda and Cindy), Russians (Dmitri, Vlad, Karla and Ana) and Indians (Rohan, Shyam, Pooja and Neha) such that there is at least one representative from each country. Neither Americans nor the Russians want their number to be less than the other in a team. A few more conditions have to be satisfied. (i) Neither Brenda nor Cindy wants to be in the same team as either Pooja or Neha. (ii) Neither Dmitri nor Vlad wants to be in the same team as either Shyam or Pooja. (iii) Michael, Karla and Rohit should not be selected together. (iv) Jack and Ana must be selected together.","setup_solution":"According to the given conditions, the possible representations from each country can be as shown below. Americans Russians Indians: (a) Two Two One. (b) One One Three. From (i) neither Brenda nor Cindy can be selected with Pooja or Neha. From (ii) neither Dmitri nor Vlad can be selected with Shyam or Pooja. From (iii) Michael, Karla and Rohit cannot be selected together. From (iv) Jack and Ana must be selected together.","entity_count":12,"variables":2,"constraints":4,"case_splits":2,"resolution_type":"multiple","information_load":"high","solving_methodologies":["conditional_logic","combinatorial_counting"],"questions":[{"id":"LR_E4B_Q016","question_text":"If Rohit is the only Indian not selected, then in how many different ways can the team be selected?","options":{"A":"One","B":"Two","C":"Three","D":"More than three"},"correct_answer":"B","correct_answer_value":"Two","solution_text":"According to case (b) above, if Rohit is the only Indian not selected, then three Indians Shyam, Pooja and Neha are selected. One each among the Americans and the Russians must be selected. From (i) and (ii), Brenda, Cindy, Dmitri and Vlad are ruled out. Hence the possible selections are (i) Shyam, Pooja, Neha, Jack, Ana (ii) Shyam, Pooja, Neha, Michael, Karla. Hence, the selections can be done in two ways.","question_operation":"count_arrangements","answer_type":"mcq","difficulty":"hard","time_benchmark_seconds":150},{"id":"LR_E4B_Q017","question_text":"If the only Indian not selected is not Rohit, then who among the following must be selected?","options":{"A":"Michael","B":"Karla","C":"Vlad","D":"Jack"},"correct_answer":"D","correct_answer_value":"Jack","solution_text":"According to case (b), if Rohit is selected, then two among Shyam, Pooja and Neha must be selected. In that case, according to conditions (i) and (ii), Brenda, Cindy, Dmitri, Vlad are ruled out. From condition (iii), Michael, Karla and Rohit cannot be selected. Hence Jack and Ana must be selected.","question_operation":"hypothetical","answer_type":"mcq","difficulty":"hard","time_benchmark_seconds":150},{"id":"LR_E4B_Q018","question_text":"If the only Indian selected is Shyam, then which among the following cannot be the pair of Americans selected?","options":{"A":"Jack, Michael","B":"Jack, Brenda","C":"Jack, Cindy","D":"Brenda, Cindy"},"correct_answer":"D","correct_answer_value":"Brenda, Cindy","solution_text":"According to case (a) above, if Shyam is the only Indian selected, then two Americans and two Russians must be selected. From (ii) Dmitri and Vlad are ruled out. Hence Karla and Ana must be selected. If Ana is selected, Jack must be selected. Among the choices, Brenda and Cindy cannot be the American pair.","question_operation":"hypothetical","answer_type":"mcq","difficulty":"hard","time_benchmark_seconds":150},{"id":"LR_E4B_Q019","question_text":"If Karla and Ana are selected, then in how many different ways can the team be selected?","options":{"A":"Six","B":"Seven","C":"Eight","D":"None of these"},"correct_answer":"B","correct_answer_value":"Seven","solution_text":"If Karla and Ana are selected, then the possible team selections are: (i) Karla, Ana, Jack, Michael, Shyam (ii) Karla, Ana, Jack, Michael, Pooja (iii) Karla, Ana, Jack, Michael, Neha (iv) Karla, Ana, Jack, Brenda, Rohit (v) Karla, Ana, Jack, Brenda, Shyam (vi) Karla, Ana, Jack, Cindy, Rohit (vii) Karla, Ana, Jack, Cindy, Shyam. Hence there are seven different ways of selecting the team.","question_operation":"count_arrangements","answer_type":"mcq","difficulty":"hard","time_benchmark_seconds":180}]},{"set_id":"LR_E4B_S20_23","exercise":"exercise_4b","type":"selections","is_set":true,"setup_text":"These questions are based on the following information. Two different teams of four persons each are to be selected from twelve persons A through L. Among them 6 persons A through F play cricket and the remaining persons play football. In a team there must be two cricketers and two football players. We have to select the team based on the following information. (i) If A is selected, then L should not be selected. (ii) If B is selected in a team, then H must be selected in the other team. (iii) If J is selected in a team, then K must be selected in the same team. (iv) Exactly one among C, D and K must be selected. (v) only if D is selected, I can be selected. (vi) At most one of D and H can be selected.","setup_solution":"As two teams, each of four players with 2 cricket players and 2 football players are to be selected. There should be exactly 4 cricket players and 4 football players. Assume that D is selected. From (iv), K should not be selected. From (iii), J should not be selected and from (vi), H should not be selected. As four football players are to be selected D should not be selected. From (v), I should not be selected. From (iii), if K is not selected, then J should not be selected which leads to the elimination of 3 football players. Hence, K must be selected. C will not be selected. From (iv), C should not be selected. Hence A, B, E and F are the four cricket players that are selected. Hence, from (i), G, H, J and K are the four football players that are selected. If L is selected, then A will not be selected, implying three cricketers are eliminated. Hence, L should not be selected. From (ii) and (iii) the possible teams: Cricket B __ ; __ __. Football J K ; H G.","entity_count":12,"variables":2,"constraints":6,"case_splits":1,"resolution_type":"multiple","resolution_count":3,"information_load":"high","solving_methodologies":["conditional_logic","constraint_elimination"],"questions":[{"id":"LR_E4B_Q020","question_text":"If K is selected in team α, then in how many ways team β can be selected?","options":{"A":"One","B":"Two","C":"Three","D":"Four"},"correct_answer":"C","correct_answer_value":"Three","solution_text":"(A, E, H, G), (A, F, H, G) and (E, F, H, G) are the three possible ways.","question_operation":"count_arrangements","answer_type":"mcq","difficulty":"hard","time_benchmark_seconds":150},{"id":"LR_E4B_Q021","question_text":"Which of the following is a possible team?","options":{"A":"JKEF","B":"EBGJ","C":"ABJH","D":"HAEG"},"correct_answer":"D","correct_answer_value":"HAEG","solution_text":"(A) JKEF: A and B must be in the other team. When B is in one team, according to (ii), H must be in the other team. This is not possible. (B) EBGJ: Condition (iii) is violated. (C) ABJH: Condition (iii) is violated. (D) HAEG: The other team can be FBGK.","question_operation":"statement_verification","answer_type":"mcq","difficulty":"hard","time_benchmark_seconds":120},{"id":"LR_E4B_Q022","question_text":"If J is selected in a team, then who among the following must be selected in that team?","options":{"A":"B","B":"E","C":"F","D":"A"},"correct_answer":"A","correct_answer_value":"B","solution_text":"B must be selected in the same team as J.","question_operation":"hypothetical","answer_type":"mcq","difficulty":"hard","time_benchmark_seconds":90},{"id":"LR_E4B_Q023","question_text":"If the persons who are not selected form a team, what is the team?","options":{"A":"CDIL","B":"CDGK","C":"AEGI","D":"None of these"},"correct_answer":"A","correct_answer_value":"CDIL","solution_text":"The players who are not selected are CDIL.","question_operation":"position_lookup","answer_type":"mcq","difficulty":"hard","time_benchmark_seconds":90}]},{"set_id":"LR_E4B_S24_26","exercise":"exercise_4b","type":"selections","is_set":true,"setup_text":"These questions are based on the following information. A team of three is to be selected from six persons – Amar, Bhavan, Chetan, Dawan, Ekta and Farheen under the following constraints. (i) If Amar or Bhavan is selected, then Chetan must not be selected. (ii) If Chetan or Dawan is selected, then at least one of Ekta and Farheen must be selected.","setup_solution":"Let each person be donated by the first letter of his name.","entity_count":6,"variables":1,"constraints":2,"case_splits":2,"resolution_type":"multiple","information_load":"low","solving_methodologies":["conditional_logic","combinatorial_counting"],"questions":[{"id":"LR_E4B_Q024","question_text":"If Dawan is selected, then who must not be selected?","options":{"A":"Amar","B":"Bhavan","C":"Chetan","D":"None of these"},"correct_answer":"D","correct_answer_value":"None of these","solution_text":"If D is selected, then some of the possibilities are: DEF, CDE, ABD. Anyone can be selected.","question_operation":"hypothetical","answer_type":"mcq","difficulty":"medium","time_benchmark_seconds":90},{"id":"LR_E4B_Q025","question_text":"If Amar is selected, then in how many ways the team can be selected?","options":{"A":"Five","B":"Six","C":"Four","D":"Seven"},"correct_answer":"A","correct_answer_value":"Five","solution_text":"If A is selected, then C must not be selected (from (i)). Now using condition (ii) the possibilities are: ABE, ABF, ADE, ADF, AEF. There are 5 possibilities.","question_operation":"count_arrangements","answer_type":"mcq","difficulty":"medium","time_benchmark_seconds":120},{"id":"LR_E4B_Q026","question_text":"If Bhavan is selected, then who must be selected?","options":{"A":"Dawan","B":"Ekta","C":"Farheen","D":"Either (B) or (C)"},"correct_answer":"D","correct_answer_value":"Either (B) or (C)","solution_text":"As B is selected, then C must not be selected. If D is selected, then E or F must be selected. If A is selected, then D must not be selected. To select a team of 3, E or F must be selected.","question_operation":"hypothetical","answer_type":"mcq","difficulty":"medium","time_benchmark_seconds":90}]},{"set_id":"LR_E4B_S27_30","exercise":"exercise_4b","type":"selections","is_set":true,"setup_text":"These questions are based on the following information. A, B, C, D and E are bowlers who play for Ranji Trophy only. Each of them has to team up with exactly one among K, L, M, N and O, who play in the national squads. The selection committee decided that one team has to be selected for each of four out of five test matches in Chennai, Kolkata, Ahmedabad, Bengaluru and Hyderabad. The following additional information is known about them: 1. No two teams are selected to play the same set of four matches. 2. K is selected for Kolkata, Ahmedabad and Bengaluru but did not team up with either C or D. 3. Each of B and N are selected for Bengaluru and Hyderabad, but are in different teams. 4. M is not paired up with either B or C. 5. N is not paired up with D or E. 6. Each of L and C is selected for Bengaluru or Hyderabad, but not both.","setup_solution":"The given conditions can be tabulated: Ranji Player - National Player - Venue. E-K: Kolkata, Ahmedabad, Bengaluru. B-O: Bengaluru, Hyderabad. A-N: Bengaluru, Hyderabad. D-M. C-L: Bengaluru or Hyderabad (not both).","entity_count":10,"variables":2,"constraints":6,"case_splits":2,"resolution_type":"single","information_load":"high","solving_methodologies":["constraint_elimination","conditional_logic"],"questions":[{"id":"LR_E4B_Q027","question_text":"If K is selected for Chennai, then C will not be selected for ______.","options":{"A":"Chennai","B":"Kolkata","C":"Ahmedabad","D":"Bengaluru"},"correct_answer":"D","correct_answer_value":"Bengaluru","solution_text":"If K is not selected for Chennai, it means K is selected for Hyderabad. Since we know that C is not selected for one city between Bengaluru and Hyderabad, he is not selected for Bengaluru.","question_operation":"hypothetical","answer_type":"mcq","difficulty":"hard","time_benchmark_seconds":120},{"id":"LR_E4B_Q028","question_text":"For which of the following matches is M definitely selected, if K is selected for Chennai?","options":{"A":"Chennai and Ahmedabad","B":"Ahmedabad and Bengaluru","C":"Bengaluru and Hyderabad","D":"Kolkata and Hyderabad"},"correct_answer":"C","correct_answer_value":"Bengaluru and Hyderabad","solution_text":"If K chooses Chennai, then he was not selected for Hyderabad, then M has to be selected for Hyderabad and Bengaluru.","question_operation":"hypothetical","answer_type":"mcq","difficulty":"hard","time_benchmark_seconds":120},{"id":"LR_E4B_Q029","question_text":"Who is paired with N?","options":{"A":"A","B":"B","C":"C","D":"Either (B) or (C)"},"correct_answer":"A","correct_answer_value":"A","solution_text":"A is the teammate.","question_operation":"position_lookup","answer_type":"mcq","difficulty":"hard","time_benchmark_seconds":90},{"id":"LR_E4B_Q030","question_text":"Which of the following statement about L is false?","options":{"A":"C is teamed up with him.","B":"L is selected for either Chennai or Kolkata.","C":"C is selected for one venue between Bengaluru and Hyderabad.","D":"C and L are selected for Chennai, Kolkata and Ahmedabad."},"correct_answer":"B","correct_answer_value":"L is selected for either Chennai or Kolkata.","solution_text":"Statement (A) is true. Statement (B) is false. Statement (C) is true. Only Statement (D) is true.","question_operation":"statement_verification","answer_type":"mcq","difficulty":"hard","time_benchmark_seconds":90}]}]');export{e as default};
